

⭐ Simulation Semantics for Atoms (CMB‑ENC Engine)

Every atom in your blueprint behaves as a typed state‑transformer acting on a global encryption state:

[ S = {D, K, A, \text{meta}, \text{cost}, \text{trace}} ]

Where:

D = data block or stream

K = key material

A = auxiliary state (nonce, counter, sponge state)

meta = structural tags

cost = performance model

trace = analysis hooks (diffusion, linearity, etc.)

Every atom implements:

[ \text{Atom}(S, \text{params}) \rightarrow S' ]

This is the heart of your simulation engine.

⭐ 1. Bit Operations

These atoms define the microscopic physics of your cipher.

Semantics

State:Apply deterministic bit‑level transform[ D' = f(D) ]

Cost:Add 1–2 cost units per word.

Trace:

Mark as linear over GF(2)

Update diffusion map (which bits influence which outputs)

Example

XOR(D, K) → D'

⭐ 2. Word Operations

These atoms give you ARX‑style behavior.

Semantics

State:Apply modular arithmetic or rotation[ D' = (D + K) \bmod 2^n ]

Cost:1–3 units depending on width.

Trace:

Mark as nonlinear over GF(2)

Update avalanche estimate

⭐ 3. Nonlinear Atoms

These atoms inject confusion, the core of symmetric security.

Semantics

State:Apply nonlinear mapping to slices of D[ D'[i..i+n] = \text{SBOX}(D[i..i+n]) ]

Cost:Table lookup or arithmetic cost.

Trace:

Add nonlinearity score

Add differential uniformity

Add algebraic degree

Update confusion metric

⭐ 4. Algebraic Structure Atoms

These atoms anchor your blueprint to a hardness class.

Semantics

State:Apply group/ring/field/lattice operations[ D' = \text{GroupOp}(D, K) ]

Cost:Architecture‑dependent (scalar mult ≫ modular add).

Trace:

Tag hardness class:

“DL over curve X”

“LWE(dim, noise)”

“Factoring modulus N”

Estimate security bits from parameters.

⭐ 5. Randomness & State Atoms

These atoms define time, entropy, and mode behavior.

Semantics

State:Update auxiliary state A

NONCE allocates

COUNTER increments

ABSORB mixes

SQUEEZE outputs

Cost:Small, except DRBG reseeds.

Trace:

Track nonce reuse risk

Track entropy budget

Track sponge state transitions

